:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tf.&#160;&#160;&#160;Rooms containing dispensing and use of hazardous materials when an explosive environment can occur because of the characteristics or nature of the hazardous materials or as a result of the dispensing or use process.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-167716\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-167716\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tg.&#160;&#160;&#160;A method of explosion control shall be provided when Class 2 water-reactive materials can form potentially explosive mixtures.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div id=\"rid-0-0-0-167717\" class=\"rbox Normal-Level\"><AnnotationDrawer recordId=\"0-0-0-167717\"><\/AnnotationDrawer><div class=\"Small\"><div style=\"margin-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt;\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\th.&#160;&#160;&#160;Explosion venting is not required for Group H-5 fabrication areas complying with the <span style=\"font-weight: normal;font-style: italic;text-decoration:none;display: inline;\">New York City Fire Code<\/span> and Section 415.11.1 of this code.<\/div><\/div><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><div class=\"clearfix\"><\/div><\/div>",
